{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Science or Science Fiction?", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Life on Mars", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Unreal Conditional: Expressing Imaginary Future Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Unreal Conditional to express imaginary or future situations. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If I knew space travel was safe, I'd be on the next ship out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Unreal Conditional is also called the second conditional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the structure: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> If\u2026 Simple Past, \u2026 would+verb  </span>or   <br> <span class=\"italic\">Would + verb \u2026 if \u2026 Simple Past</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> If scientists knew for sure they wouldn't have to keep looking for answers.</span> <br> Scientists can't know for sure, so they probably have to keep looking for answers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use  <span class=\"italic\"> If \u2026 were + to + infinitive </span> to talk about imaginary future situations, especially when it is not likely the situation will happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">If you were to stand in a crowded area and watch the people, what would you see?</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Would it be too late for me to travel through the galaxy if it were to happen soon?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For me it's probably too late, but for many others, if the technology were to become available, they ,like me, would be thinking of going too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If scientists knew for sure they wouldn't have to keep looking for answers.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Verbs Followed by -ing with Objects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you talk about two actions linked together, you normally use two verbs. The first verb follows the rules of conjugation for the sentence, while the second verb can be a verb in the -ing form.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Have you overheard people speaking of astronauts with envy?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can use two verbs to talk about two connected actions. The main verb introduces the main action, and the second verb in the -ing form gives more information about that action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use a variety of verbs followed by a verb in the -ing form. Some of these verbs are related in meaning, or have opposite meanings, like: <br><span class=\"italic\"> like/dislike, start/stop, can't bear/stand, love/adore/hate, allow/forbid, admit/deny, quit/finish, appreciate/resent ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can often put an object between the two verbs. You can use pronouns and possessives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br> Subject + first verb + object + -ing form of the second verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> Have you ever observed someone gazing into the night sky with longing?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have you caught scientists talking about looking for proof of life on other planets?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How many times have you watched people hanging on every word of science fiction movie? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Has it ever left you wondering who or what else is out there?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Have you ever noticed comets hurtling through the night sky and wondered what it would look like up close? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to gaze ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at something for a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you ever observed someone gazing into the night sky with longing?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Mars.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to overhear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hear what people are saying without intending to, and without their knowledge", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you overheard people speaking of astronauts with envy? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comet ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a body of rock and ice that travels around the sun", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you ever noticed comets hurtling through the night sky and wondered what it would look like up close?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hurtle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move very fast ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you ever noticed comets hurtling through the night sky and wondered what it would look like up close?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hard evidence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "physical, measurable proof", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Until recently, however, no one had discovered hard evidence that living things ever existed on another planet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meteorite ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "rock from \u200bspace that has \u200blanded on \u200bEarth ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A meteorite found on a scientific expedition to Antarctica in 1984 suggested that there might once have been life on another planet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "red planet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "another name for Mars", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today they are still looking to the red planet for signs of life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "manned mission", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a human crew of explorers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Would they put together a manned mission if they had some answers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the film The Martian to find out about a mission to Mars.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes on what people will have to overcome to be able to exist on the red planet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a group, discuss what you have noted, saying whether you believe these things are or are not possible to overcome.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss how you feel about manned missions to Mars in general and whether you think anyone could survive one and continue to live on Mars.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch the film <span class=\"italic\">The Martian</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes on what people will have to overcome to be able to exist on the red planet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the hardships of a manned mission to Mars with a partner or group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le04ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about science and exploration.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about imaginary situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about two actions together.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you know about the planet Mars?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Would you be interested in going on a manned mission to Mars?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Was there ever life on Mars?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1