: "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "If I knew space travel was safe, I'd be on the next ship out. Would it be too late for me to travel through the galaxy if it were to happen soon? For me probably, not for many others, if the technology were to become available, they, like me, would be thinking of going too. Have you ever observed someone gazing into the night sky with longing? Have you overheard people speaking of astronauts with envy?  Have you caught scientists talking about looking for proof of life on other planets?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": ""}, {"text": "How many times have you watched people hanging on every word of science fiction movies? Have you ever noticed comets hurtling through the night sky and wondered what it would look like up close? Has it ever left you wondering who or what else is out there? Until recently, however, no one had discovered hard evidence that living things ever existed on another planet. A meteorite found on a scientific expedition to Antarctica in 1984 suggested that there might once have been life on another planet. A NASA scientific team studied the 4.25-pound meteorite for twelve years.", "id": 2, "time": "29000", "image": ""}, {"text": "They estimated the rock's age at 4.5 billion years. Could it have been from Mars? If scientists knew for sure, they wouldn't have to keep looking for answers. Today they are still looking to the red planet for signs of life. What would they do  if they found it?  Would they put together a manned mission if they had some answers? If you were still following such inquiries, they might be answered sometime after 2024 when the first Mars Mission leaves Earth.", "id": 3, "time": "66000", "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn11le04ob05re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "_data": [], "type": "video", "template_override": 1}]}]}